## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design scalable, tenant-aware ML pipelines with calibration, streaming features, drift handling, and safe rollout strategies across enterprise-scale tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant feature stores and leakage prevention
- Shared base model + per-tenant calibrator
- Real-time features from streaming usage and billing
- Online retraining with drift detectors
- Offline + online evaluation and staged rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo calibration hook
function calibrate(probs, tenantId, store){
  const params = store.getParams(tenantId)
  // adjust by temp scaler
  return Math.min(0.999, Math.max(0.001, probs * params.scale + params.bias))
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant calibration offline and online?
- How would you guard against cross-tenant data leakage in CV and feature drift?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design real-time systems for graph-structured streaming data, balancing ultra-low latency, accuracy, privacy, and drift handling in a production-grade payments platform.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming graph features and two-tier detection pipelines
- Privacy-preserving techniques (secure aggregation, differential privacy)
- Drift detection (ADWIN, population stability index), model calibration
- End-to-end pipeline: event ingestion, feature extraction, scoring, alerting, and feedback loop
- Canary rollout strategies and A/B testing for model deployment

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreEvent(event, fastModel, deepModel) {
  const features = fastModel.extractFeatures(event);
  const fastScore = fastModel.predict(features);

  if (fastScore > fastModel.threshold) {
    queueEventForDeepAnalysis(event);
    return { alert: true, score: fastScore, deepAnalysis: 'pending' };
  }

  return { alert: false, score: fastScore };
}

async function deepAnalysis(event) {
  const graphContext = await fetchGraphContext(event.entityId);
  const deepFeatures = deepModel.buildFeatures(event, graphContext);
  return deepModel.predict(deepFeatures);
}
```
